# WN22-DC-000040: Windows Server 2022 Kerberos user ticket lifetime must be limited to 10 hours or less.
# Source: Windows Server 2022 STIG r8
# Severity: medium
# Generated from 01-extract/output/windows-server-2022-stig-r8-controls.json

META
    esp_id `win2022-wn22-dc-000040-001`
    version `1.0.0`
    dsl_schema_version `1.0.0`
    platform `windows`
    criticality `high`

    title `Windows Server 2022 Kerberos user ticket lifetime must be limited to 10 hours or less.`
    description `In Kerberos, there are two types of tickets: Ticket Granting Tickets (TGTs) and Service Tickets. Kerberos tickets have a limited lifetime so the time an attacker has to implement an attack is limited. This policy controls how long TGTs can be renewed. With Kerberos, the user's initial authentication to the domain controller results in a TGT, which is then used to request Service Tickets to resources. Upon startup, each computer gets a TGT before requesting a service ticket to the domain controll`
    author `scanset-security`
    tags `windows,server-2022,stig,medium,kerberos-policy,security-policy,ksi-iam-apm,ksi-iam-mfa`

    control_mapping `KSI:KSI-IAM-APM,KSI:KSI-IAM-MFA,NIST-800-53:IA-2(8)`
    control_objective `KSI-IAM-APM,KSI-IAM-MFA`

    assessment_method `TEST`
    implementation_status `implemented`
    responsible_role `system-admin`

    control_origination `sp-system`
    inherited_from `Windows:server-2022:endpoint`
    customer_responsibility `configuration`

    remediation_days `30`
    recommendation `Configure the policy value in the Default Domain Policy for Computer Configuration >> Policies >> Windows Settings >> Security Settings >> Account Policies >> Kerberos Policy >> Maximum lifetime for user ticket to a maximum of "10" hours but not "0", which equates to "Ticket doesn't expire".`

    component_id `comp-windows-security-policy`

    impl_KSI_IAM_APM `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-APM by enforcing MaxTicketAge per the STIG (Kerberos user ticket maximum lifetime must be 1-10 hours.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_KSI_IAM_MFA `Windows Server implements KSI-IAM-MFA by enforcing MaxTicketAge per the STIG (Kerberos user ticket maximum lifetime must be 1-10 hours.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`
    impl_IA_2_8 `Windows Server implements IA-2(8) by enforcing MaxTicketAge per the STIG (Kerberos user ticket maximum lifetime must be 1-10 hours.). The ESP scanner queries the policy via the windows_security_policy CTN and fails the policy if the value does not match the STIG-required state. Remediation sets the policy via secedit or Group Policy.`

META_END

DEF
    OBJECT target
        policy_name `MaxTicketAge`
    OBJECT_END

    STATE compliant
        exists boolean = true
        value_int int >= 1
        value_int int <= 10
    STATE_END

    CRI AND
        CTN windows_security_policy
            TEST all all AND
            STATE_REF compliant
            OBJECT_REF target
        CTN_END
    CRI_END
DEF_END
